From: SJ Park <sj@kernel.org>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:28:03 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] mm/damon/core: remove damon_{en,dis}able_report_producer()

For now, user report is the only supported type.  If we will have a
global report queue, the APIs for producer enablement is not needed.
When we have new report type, which will call damon_submit_report() on
thier own, we may need the API functions.  But, not for now.  Remove
those.

Signed-off-by: SJ Park <sj@kernel.org>
---
 include/linux/damon.h |  2 --
 mm/damon/core.c       | 10 ----------
 2 files changed, 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/linux/damon.h b/include/linux/damon.h
index d7aa9bd86cd48..0467ae48dc539 100644
--- a/include/linux/damon.h
+++ b/include/linux/damon.h
@@ -1352,8 +1352,6 @@ int damon_kdamond_pid(struct damon_ctx *ctx);
 int damon_call(struct damon_ctx *ctx, struct damon_call_control *control);
 int damos_walk(struct damon_ctx *ctx, struct damos_walk_control *control);
 
-int damon_enable_report_producer(enum damon_report_type, unsigned int id);
-int damon_disable_report_producer(unsigned int id);
 int damon_submit_report(struct damon_report *report);
 
 void damon_report_access(struct damon_access_report *report);
diff --git a/mm/damon/core.c b/mm/damon/core.c
index 94413223b2a82..db8478f8461ff 100644
--- a/mm/damon/core.c
+++ b/mm/damon/core.c
@@ -2512,16 +2512,6 @@ int damos_walk(struct damon_ctx *ctx, struct damos_walk_control *control)
 	return 0;
 }
 
-int damon_enable_report_producer(enum damon_report_type, unsigned int id)
-{
-	return 0;
-}
-
-int damon_disable_report_producer(unsigned int id)
-{
-	return 0;
-}
-
 int damon_submit_report(struct damon_report *report)
 {
 	return 0;
-- 
2.47.3

